INT. NIGHT LAUNDROMAT - 3 A.M.

Fluorescent hum. Dryers turning. Rain on the glass.

NADIA REYES, 30s, folds a hospital scrub top with exact corners. Alone.

The bell above the door chimes. A STRANGER, 40s, wet raincoat, enters. Sits two machines away. Stares.

NADIA
We close at four.

STRANGER
I know.

GUS, 60s, the attendant, leans out from the back office, mop in hand.

GUS
Everything okay out here?

NADIA
Fine, Gus.

STRANGER
Gus. Right.

GUS
Do I know you?

STRANGER
You know her.

Nadia stops folding.

NADIA
I don't know you.

STRANGER
You knew my brother.

GUS
Hey, pal --

NADIA
Which brother?

STRANGER
The one in the chart. Room 412.

GUS
Hey, pal, you're done. Out.

STRANGER
Oskar. His name was Oskar. Say it.

Nadia sets the scrub top down. Her hands shake.

NADIA
Oskar --

OSKAR
(Stranger, now standing)
Not him. Me. I'm Oskar. He was Anton.

GUS
Nadia, back away from --

OSKAR
She signed the form, Gus.

Gus raises the mop. Oskar pulls a folded paper from his coat. Slaps it onto the machine.

Every dryer stops spinning. Silence.
